flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4f4ddcad09956d609f463a7803f8261a152c2def","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/zkIE/commits/4f4ddcad09956d609f463a7803f8261a152c2def","html_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/zkIE/commit/4f4ddcad09956d609f463a7803f8261a152c2def"},{"sha":"9b27dbdf68cb308784d4d3af05f5a38d485543e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/zkIE/commits/9b27dbdf68cb308784d4d3af05f5a38d485543e3","html_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/zkIE/commit/9b27dbdf68cb308784d4d3af05f5a38d485543e3"}],"stats":{"total":17,"additions":11,"deletions":6},"files":[{"sha":"2518261345fa898c9c0142e9380dc1d7c3acc758","filename":"README.md","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":3,"changes":10,"blob_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/zkIE/blob/39d8df96877bc3bebf33c69b06907d792b3184b9/README.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/zkIE/raw/39d8df96877bc3bebf33c69b06907d792b3184b9/README.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/zkIE/contents/README.md?ref=39d8df96877bc3bebf33c69b06907d792b3184b9","patch":"@@ -30,9 +30,13 @@ time and memory, both still far above the cost of the inference itself.\n **How it is used.** Export the model to ONNX — architecture, weights and op\n graph — and zkIE composes the proving logic for that model's inference circuit\n out of op-level proof primitives. For any input, that circuit then yields a\n-succinct proof that the output is what the model computes; verifying it is cheap\n-and does not re-run the model. Weights and activations are public: the current\n-route targets correctness and succinctness rather than witness hiding.\n+proof that the output is what the model computes. Today the verifier still\n+recomputes the forward pass to obtain its interior evaluations (`verify_shard` /\n+`verify_shard_dag`, `compose.rs`), so verifying costs about as much as proving\n+(measured: verify ~90% of prove at seq=512, CPU); making verification succinct,\n+with no re-run, is the open design item tracked in #15. Weights and activations\n+are public: the current route targets correctness and succinctness rather than\n+witness hiding.\n \n ## How it works\n "},{"sha":"14acdcb5b97bade20dbc508dbf62ef2d5fa13961","filename":"docs/roadmap.md","status":"modified","additions":4,"deletions":3,"changes":7,"blob_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/zkIE/blob/39d8df96877bc3bebf33c69b06907d792b3184b9/docs%2Froadmap.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/trustless-ai/zkIE/raw/39d8df96877bc3bebf33c69b06907d792b3184b9/docs%2Froadmap.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/trustless-ai/zkIE/contents/docs%2Froadmap.md?ref=39d8df96877bc3bebf33c69b06907d792b3184b9","patch":"@@ -54,9 +54,10 @@ New capabilities to prove:\n    routing. Memory scales with *active* parameters, not total. This is the only\n    lever that lets MoE scale.\n 3. **op list built per-forward from the route** - the static chain becomes a\n-   data-dependent chain. Since a proof is already for one concrete forward and\n-   the verifier only checks the proof (does not re-run), this only changes the\n-   build flow, not the proof abstraction.\n+   data-dependent chain. Since a proof is already for one concrete forward, this\n+   only changes the build flow, not the proof abstraction. (The verifier currently\n+   recomputes that forward to read interior evaluations; succinct verification,\n+   with no re-run, is tracked in #15.)\n \n Expected order of magnitude (extrapolated from current calibration):\n prove ~10-14 min (seq=512), peak memory ~50-150 GB (fully-resident commitment"}]}